    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="1017" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-09T18:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>524. Department’s 330 via Paris.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d738-f1"/> Acknowledging
                    receipt of <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> handed by me to Lord Curzon
                    on October 30, Foreign Office states in note dated November 8 that British
                    Government “will welcome the presence of one or more United States
                    representatives at Lausanne for the purposes indicated.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d738-f1" n="14" xml:id="d738-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 344, Oct. 27, to the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg884"
                        >p. 884</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
